# Test: OSPFv2 Segment Routing Adj-SID lifecycle (spec-ospf-ext-5 AC-12/AC-13, RFC 8665 §7.4.1).
#
# VALIDATES: an Adj-SID is allocated from the SRLB when a neighbor reaches Full and installs a
# pop/forward mpls-fib entry toward that neighbor; dropping below 2-Way withdraws the entry and
# frees the SRLB label.
# PREVENTS: a stale pop entry to a dead neighbor, or an SRLB label leak.

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=go test -v ./internal/plugins/ospf -run TestSRAdjSIDAllocatedAtFull|TestSRAdjSIDWithdrawnBelow2Way|TestSRLANAdjSIDCarriesNeighborID -count=1:timeout=90s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=PASS
